:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:128:\"As the Coalition shows its colours on nature, Labor faces a question: will it really protect Australia’s wildlife? | Clear Air\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:162:\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/oct/25/as-the-coalition-shows-its-colours-on-nature-labor-faces-a-question-will-it-really-protect-australias-wildlife\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:1608:\"<p>There are some decent elements in what Labor is proposing, but the overhaul could end up as tinkering rather than transformation</p><ul><li><p>Want to get this in your inbox when it publishes?<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/mar/10/sign-up-for-the-clear-air-australia-environment-newsletter-with-adam-morton?CMP=cvau_sfl\"> Sign up for the Clear Air Australia newsletter here</a></p></li></ul><p>In an age of monumental political shifts, the news that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/oct/23/labors-environment-law-revamp-in-jeopardy-as-coalition-dubs-it-hand-brake-on-investment\">the Coalition doesn’t like</a>, and very likely won’t support, Labor’s proposed revamp of national nature law has at least had one thing going for it. It is achingly predictable.</p><p>I mean … of course it was going to go this way. Australia’s rightwing parties are a mess, and threatening to tear themselves apart. It’s possible not every Coalition MP dismisses the evidence that the country’s extraordinary and unique environment is in long-term decline. But a significant number do.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/mar/10/sign-up-for-the-clear-air-australia-environment-newsletter-with-adam-morton?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up to get climate and environment editor Adam Morton’s Clear Air column as a free newsletter</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/oct/25/as-the-coalition-shows-its-colours-on-nature-labor-faces-a-question-will-it-really-protect-australias-wildlife\">Continue reading...</a>\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:7:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:11:\"Environment\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:51:\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/environment\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"Australia news\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:57:\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/australia-news\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"Climate crisis\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:54:\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:3;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"Australian politics\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:62:\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/australian-politics\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:4;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:9:\"Coalition\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:52:\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/coalition\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:5;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:11:\"Labor party\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:6:\"domain\";s:54:\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/labor-party\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:6;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:17:\"Austra